BASILISK_VOCAB_MODULE_WORD='service'
BASILISK_VOCAB_HELP_INTRO='Basalt -- runs a Basalt deployment: the standard one runs an
interactive console (Emacs), two engine services (Gendl on CCL and on
SBCL), and a monitor (autoheal), joined on one Docker network and
health-validated.  Anything more (an ingress, licensed engine variants)
arrives by overlay: a *-stack repo installed beside this one.

Services answer to their names (listed under SERVICES below);
containers carry a generated instance name, fresh at every full start
(read them with '\''%s status'\'', or from .muster).
%s and ./compose-dev are the same file, so nothing that
already says compose-dev breaks.  See BASALT.md and README.md.'
BASILISK_VOCAB_HELP_CMD_UP='Start the deployment, or named services only (default: all)'
BASILISK_VOCAB_HELP_CMD_DOWN='Stop and remove the whole deployment'
BASILISK_VOCAB_HELP_CMD_RESTART='Restart one service, or all'
BASILISK_VOCAB_HELP_CMD_STOP='Stop without removing containers'
BASILISK_VOCAB_HELP_CMD_LOGS='A service'\''s logs'
BASILISK_VOCAB_HELP_CMD_STATUS='Each service, its instance name, and its health'
BASILISK_VOCAB_HELP_CMD_EMACS='Attach an emacsclient terminal to the console'
